meta {
  name: code graph status
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/codegraph/status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~sessionId: {{sessionId}}
}

docs {
  Whether graphify is on the server's tool PATH (with the folders searched and the install line) and, with a sessionId, whether that session's working folder has graphify-out/graph.html (its time) and the folder's last build since the server started (card 472). The folder is the live session's resolved workspace or, for a stored session not continued yet, the folder its own record names. Without sessionId it answers the installation alone, which the doctor panel reads. 200, 400 malformed sessionId, 404 unknown session.
  
  Fence: host. Loopback fence: the TCP peer must be loopback AND the Host header must be localhost/127.0.0.1/::1. A REST client passes automatically when it targets http://localhost:<port>. A LAN IP or rebound DNS name in the URL answers a blank 404.
  
  Writes state: no
}
